A||N||9||bcwawright||Fron Wheel Drive Getrag||||5||
Z||000000||bcwawright||05-29-2001||12:17 PM||||Could someone tell me which front wheel drive cars(make, model, and year) came with a 5sp Getrag. I need to go salvage hunting for a transaxle.<BR>Thanks in advance for any help.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||05-29-2001||12:24 PM||||Any FWD 5spd V6 except the Quad 4 trans. Won't fit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||05-29-2001||01:00 PM||||Well thats confusion. The ones with the quad wont fit or the ones without wont fit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||05-29-2001||01:53 PM||||Look for Berettas, Cavaliers, etc. with a V-6 (same era as the Fiero.....late 80's/early 90's).<P>To clarify.....don't use the Getrags from those cars that came with a quad 4.....the bolt pattern is different and they won't bolt to the Fiero engine.  <P>You will need to use Rodneys conversion kit, but it isn't much $$.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||05-29-2001||03:37 PM||||Mrfiero is right, unless of course you have a Quad-4 in your Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||05-29-2001||04:04 PM||||There are several different types of FWD Getrags. I have three of them and each one is different. If you find one from a early Z-24 with a cable driven speedometer, you won't need to split the case to install a VSS drive gear.||||reg||1
Z||000006||p4n1c||05-29-2001||04:13 PM||||My car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It had a 5-spd Getrag transmission available for it I believe.<P>Some information on the Getrag as of 1989: <P>HM-282 (5TM40)<BR>200 lb/ft maximum torque<BR>88 lbs. dry weight<BR>7000 RPM Maximum input speed<P><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Taijiguy||05-29-2001||04:57 PM||||If you're creative, you can fabricate shifter brackets, and keep the four speed cables. Use the cable holding brackets from the four speed. Saves buying/pulling/replacing the cables. Also, the five speed shifter is different from the four speed in that it has no detents. So you can really modify the four speed shifter as well, if your fabbing skills are even marginal.||||reg||14
Z||000008||terryk||05-29-2001||05:59 PM||||I thought it was intuitively obvious to the most casual observer.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000009||rockcrawl||05-29-2001||06:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>you can fabricate shifter brackets, and keep the four speed cables. Use the cable holding brackets from the four speed. Saves buying/pulling/replacing the cables<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Hmmm.. that's good to know, I've been considering using a Getrag in my 4 spped car. It sounds like you've already done it, what did u use for the slave cyl and bracket?||||reg||1
